{
  "_doc": "Shell commands and the action tokens every command classifier must give them: the proxy's actions.rs, @intutic/gate's actions.ts, intutic-clawde's gate/actions.py and the hook gates' hold classifier (gateBody.ts). Each implementation compares only the tokens it produces: the hold classifier knows deploy, publish, release and db_write. notHeld commands classify to none of them. Every space in a pattern stands for whatever the shell or the database reads as a word break: SQL_GAP in actions.rs, the phrase matcher (shared-types phrases.ts, phrases.py) everywhere else. adversarial lists [unit, times] inputs every JavaScript and Python implementation must classify in under 200 ms: nothing may backtrack on them.",
  "held": [
    ["git push origin main", ["action:deploy"]],
    ["psql -c \"DROP TABLE users\"", ["action:db_write"]],
